   "source": [
    "**Outlier takeaways**\n",
    "- **`z2_AC3` and `z2_AC4` are effectively dead** — ~0.01 kW nearly 100% of the time (standby/meter noise). Treat them as\n",
    "  unused units; drop them from modelling (they carry no signal) but keep them in totals (negligible).\n",
    "- A handful of **single-minute spikes** (e.g. 4,762 kW, 798 kW) are sensor glitches → set to NaN.\n",
    "- **28–31 Aug 2018** shows simultaneous, sustained high readings on lighting, z1_Plug and AC1 — including overnight.\n",
    "  It's multi-hour and consistent across meters, so it looks like a **real event** (e.g. an event / after-hours use of the space)\n",
    "  rather than noise. Kept in the data, but worth flagging when building a baseline."
   ]
  },
