    "## 12. Findings summary & next steps\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data structure**\n",
    "- 790,560 rows (Jul 2018 – Dec 2019), perfectly regular 1-minute timeline; both files share the same 11 power meters.\n",
    "- Floor 1 has **power only**: 4 lighting zones (z1–z4), 3 plug zones (z1–z3), 4 AC units (all in z2). No temperature, humidity or lux.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data quality**\n",
    "- Missingness is low (<0.6%) except **z2_Plug: a ~20-day outage, 22 Aug – 11 Sep 2018** (11% of 2018). Don't interpolate it.\n",
    "- 67 logger-wide outage blocks (all meters NaN), longest ≈ 5 h (17 Aug 2018) and ≈ 4.5 h (12–13 Jul 2019).\n",
    "- A few order-of-magnitude single-minute glitches (z3_Light 4,762 kW, z2_AC2 798 kW, z4_Light 512 kW, z2_AC3 25 kW) → removed.\n",
    "- **z2_AC3 and z2_AC4 never run** (~0.01 kW 99.7% of the time): dead or unused units, so exclude them from modelling.\n",
    "- **28–31 Aug 2018**: sustained, simultaneous high load on lighting, z1_Plug and AC1. Looks like a real event, not noise; flag it when building a baseline.\n",
    "- ⚠️ **Timestamps look ~7 h ahead of local time** (section 7). This affects every hour-of-day / weekday result.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Consumption**\n",
    "- Average floor draw ≈ 107 kW. **Lighting is the largest end-use (~52%)**, then AC (~31%), plugs (~17%).\n",
    "- Zone 2 dominates (~55%) because it holds all the AC plus the biggest plug load.\n",
    "- Monthly energy ranges ~66–98 MWh; peaks in Jul–Aug 2018 and May 2019 (AC-driven; hottest months in Bangkok).\n",
    "- **AC1 is the workhorse** (on ~73% of minutes, ~45 kW when on); **AC2 is a supplementary unit** that runs more in hot months\n",
    "  (30–43% of minutes in Apr–May, <5% in Nov–Dec 2019).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Year-over-year (Jul–Dec 2018 vs Jul–Dec 2019): total load −17%**\n",
    "- **z2_Light dropped ~52% as a step change around mid-Feb 2019** (≈14.7 → 7.3 kW). Looks like a retrofit (e.g. LED) or a schedule change, which makes it a clean natural experiment for a savings/baseline question.\n",
    "- **z1_Plug fell ~65%** and is near zero from Oct 2019. Equipment may have been removed or the space vacated.\n",
    "- AC is also down ~16% (AC2 used much less in late 2019).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Correlations (hourly)**\n",
    "- Weak overall. The strongest is z1_Light ↔ z4_Light (r ≈ 0.66), and AC1 tracks z4_Light (r ≈ 0.49), suggesting a shared occupancy schedule.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Possible project directions from Floor 1**\n",
    "1. Measurement & verification: quantify savings from the Feb 2019 z2_Light step change against a pre-change baseline.\n",
    "2. Anomaly detection: the Aug 2018 event, spikes and outages are useful labelled examples.\n",
    "3. Load forecasting of AC1 / total load (seasonality + weekly schedule), once the timestamp question is settled.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Next steps**\n",
    "- [ ] Compare the timestamp inversion with the other floors (group decision on a correction)\n",
    "- [ ] Check whether a retrofit on Floor 1 around Feb 2019 is documented anywhere\n",
    "- [ ] Pull outdoor weather (Bangkok temperature) to explain AC seasonality, since Floor 1 has no indoor temp sensor"
   ]
